import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 535 | Historical-Reversal Simulation · Tang-Luo World — Collapse Trajectory of the Bounty System","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 535 | Historical-Reversal Simulation · Tang-Luo World — Collapse Trajectory of the Bounty System","no":535,"module":3,"tags":["Historical-Reversal Simulation","Tang-Luo","Bounty System","Reversal Trajectory","Quest-Domain Simulation Review"],"related":["84-Archaeology Protocol General Outline","87-Knowledge-Only Return Principle","04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis","22-Joint-Contracting Resource-Distribution Mechanism"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0535_模块3-历史倒车模拟-唐罗世界-恩赐制崩溃轨迹.md","filePath":"en/0535_模块3-历史倒车模拟-唐罗世界-恩赐制崩溃轨迹.md"}'),r={name:"en/0535_模块3-历史倒车模拟-唐罗世界-恩赐制崩溃轨迹.md"};function a(s,e,l,u,h,c){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-535-historical-reversal-simulation-·-tang-luo-world-—-collapse-trajectory-of-the-bounty-system" tabindex="-1">Entry 535 | Historical-Reversal Simulation · Tang-Luo World — Collapse Trajectory of the Bounty System <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-535-historical-reversal-simulation-·-tang-luo-world-—-collapse-trajectory-of-the-bounty-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 535 | Historical-Reversal Simulation · Tang-Luo World — Collapse Trajectory of the Bounty System&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain Civilizational-Experience System | Benchmark base: Documents 84, 87, 04, 22</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-the-bountifier-leaves-what-keeps-the-whole-system-going" tabindex="-1">Introduction: when the bountifier leaves, what keeps the whole system going <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-the-bountifier-leaves-what-keeps-the-whole-system-going" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: when the bountifier leaves, what keeps the whole system going&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Tang Luo system is a typical example repeatedly dissected in Module 2: a strong one of the Gu Chensha style distributes cultivation resources as &quot;bounty&quot;; supporting roles enter by receiving rewards; mortals outside the system survive or die on their own. This structure looks efficient in the bountifier&#39;s prime, but buried a time bomb: <strong>bounty is one-way, privately bestowed, shifts with the bountifier&#39;s will.</strong> The historical-reversal simulation must answer a cold and clear question — once the bountifier leaves (falls, disappears, no longer cares), along what curve does the Tang-Luo world reverse on the time axis?</p><p>Six top-level axioms are this review&#39;s highest criteria: anti-predation axiom wants us to see through that the bounty system&#39;s essence is still &quot;the strong monopolizing distribution&quot;; republican axiom of Myriad Races wants us to count the vast majority blocked out under the bounty system; collective ascension axiom contrasts the bounty system&#39;s fate of &quot;the strong alone reaching the top; all beings marking time&quot;; causal self-discipline axiom constrains the whole simulation to run only in Quest-Sediment-Domain sandboxes, only knowledge returned without perturbing real planes; law-first axiom requires every step of the collapse trajectory deduced first by institution-energy causal chains, not plot-driven sudden collapse. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-three-layers-of-fragility-in-the-bounty-system" tabindex="-1">I. Three Layers of Fragility in the Bounty System <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-three-layers-of-fragility-in-the-bounty-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Three Layers of Fragility in the Bounty System&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In the sandbox, the Tang-Luo world&#39;s institutions are restored to three layers; each layer has a clear reversal fuse:</p><ol><li><strong>Distribution-layer fragility</strong>: cultivation resources distributed by the bountifier&#39;s personal will, not joint-contracting more-work-more-pay (Document 22). Once the bountifier leaves, resource distribution immediately stalls; no one knows &quot;who gets the next reward.&quot;</li><li><strong>Knowledge-layer fragility</strong>: core techniques opened per the bountifier&#39;s mood; the Great Dao not publicly systematized. Recipients learned &quot;results&quot; not &quot;principles&quot;; once the wrong person is entrusted, knowledge is immediately lost.</li><li><strong>Heart-layer fragility</strong>: all beings&#39; expectation of the bountifier is built on the assumption &quot;he will always reward.&quot; Once this assumption breaks, gratitude reverses into resentment in very short order; order collapses from within.</li></ol><h2 id="ii-the-collapse-curve-five-stages" tabindex="-1">II. The Collapse Curve: Five Stages <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-collapse-curve-five-stages" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Collapse Curve: Five Stages&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Sandbox deduction shows the bounty system&#39;s reversal is not a cliff, but a five-segment sliding curve:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Time-Axis Manifestation</th><th>Social Signs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>I. Reward Vacuum</td><td>First generation after bountifier disappears</td><td>Panic at the top; scramble for stock resources begins</td></tr><tr><td>II. Private Bestowal</td><td>Second generation</td><td>Strong ones each recruit favorites; &quot;little bountifiers&quot; sprout everywhere</td></tr><tr><td>III. Law Disorder</td><td>Third generation</td><td>Old bounty order replaced by jungle law; private vengeance rampant</td></tr><tr><td>IV. Knowledge Break</td><td>Fourth to fifth generations</td><td>Core techniques completely lost; cultivation regresses to bloodline secret transmission</td></tr><tr><td>V. Full Degeneration</td><td>After tenth generation</td><td>Civilization degenerates into tribal warfare; even &quot;there once was a bountifier&quot; becomes myth</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The curve&#39;s most noteworthy point is <strong>Stage II</strong>: it does not immediately descend into chaos, but breaks the great bountifier into countless little bountifiers — this is precisely the breeding ground of &quot;enlightened predators&quot; and &quot;righteous scoundrels.&quot; All beings&#39; original-sin craving for shortcuts erupts centrally in this stage; everyone wants to be the next bountifier; no one wants to build true republicanism.</p><h2 id="iii-control-experiment-with-the-joint-contracting-system" tabindex="-1">III. Control Experiment With the Joint-Contracting System <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-control-experiment-with-the-joint-contracting-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Control Experiment With the Joint-Contracting System&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In the same sandbox, researchers ran a control: replace the bounty system with joint-contracting more-work-more-pay (Document 22) and all-level Great-Dao openness; other conditions unchanged. Result: the time vector stayed positive; even amid resource crises, civilization self-repaired via incremental development and open knowledge iteration, no reversal ever again. Two control groups clearly prove: <strong>the root of Tang-Luo reversal is not &quot;the bountifier is not strong enough,&quot; but that the distribution system ties civilization&#39;s lifeline to one person.</strong></p><p>This also from the reverse confirms the Tang-Luo &quot;extremely high protagonist-uniqueness dependence&quot; verdict: a single-pillar system; once the single pillar falls, the mansion topples.</p><h2 id="iv-review-results-three-institutional-patches" tabindex="-1">IV. Review Results: Three Institutional Patches <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-review-results-three-institutional-patches" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Review Results: Three Institutional Patches&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The sandbox distills the collapse lessons into three patches directly usable in Civilizational Correction Engineering:</p><ul><li><strong>Depersonalize distribution</strong>: no civilization may tie key resource distribution to a single strong one; must have institutional distribution mechanisms as backstop.</li><li><strong>De-bounty knowledge</strong>: the Great Dao and core techniques must be publicly systematized, written as texts anyone can self-learn, not &quot;tailor-made&quot; rewards.</li><li><strong>De-heroify power</strong>: governance relies on the four-power checks of the Anchor Deliberative Council, Symbiotic Executive Committee, Symbiotic Court, Anchor Supervisory Committee (Document 49), not a super hero as backstop.</li></ul><p>All three generated within isolated sandboxes, following the &quot;Knowledge-Only Return Principle&quot; (Document 87), not perturbing a causal hair of the real Tang-Luo plane.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the bounty system wastes top strong ones&#39; mental energy on &quot;reward distribution&quot; that institutions could automate; the sandbox proves this is civilizational-level energy waste</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: bounty looks kind; its essence is soft predation of monopolized distribution; the reversal curve proves it dies slower and more unjustly than hard predation</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: this article is Tang-Luo&#39;s own reversal dissection — its upper limit is not &quot;can a stronger protagonist appear,&quot; but &quot;what happens when the protagonist is gone&quot;</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the review registers mortals and foreign races deprived of evolutionary qualification under the bounty system one by one, verifying 99% coverage necessity</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: collapse-curve model, three institutional patches openly filed, for all symbiotic planes&#39; self-check</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Tang-Luo world&#39;s reversal simulation teaches all civilizations that &quot;pin hope on one super hero&quot; the cruelest lesson: bounty can buy momentary prosperity, but cannot buy institutional continuation. When a civilization must rely on one person being ever-present to avoid regression, it has actually already begun regressing — just not yet seen.</p><p>In the final analysis, the Tang-Luo bounty-system collapse trajectory described in this document is no isolated case — it runs within Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s overall coordinates; its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./84-考古协议总纲.html">84-Archaeology Protocol General Outline</a> · <a href="./87-仅回传知识原则.html">87-Knowledge-Only Return Principle</a> · <a href="./04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis</a> · <a href="./22-资源分配联产承包机制.html">22-Joint-Contracting Resource-Distribution Mechanism</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',26)])])}const p=t(r,[["render",a]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
